 "The paper's thesis is that a personality trait in a language model is a single linear direction in its activations, extractable by one automated pipeline from nothing but a trait's name and a short description, and usable as a dial to steer the trait, a gauge to read it before or after training, and a filter to catch the training data that would induce it — demonstrated across evil, sycophancy, and hallucination on two open chat models.",
 "The 2025 argument: a trait is a direction, found automatically and dosed",
